The release ships the files we add to the browser tree.

Both of upstream's copy steps enumerate what reaches the built product, and
neither knows about files this fork adds. Left alone each fails the same silent
way: the file is present in the source tree, absent from the release, and the
page that references it 404s at runtime with nothing failing at build time.

  ci/build/build-release.sh   src/browser/pages is filtered to *.html and *.css,
                              which is right for what that directory means
                              upstream - templates and their styles. Ours also
                              holds the scripts those templates load (auth.js,
                              favicon.js, password-check.js), all served from
                              /_static, and this is the only step that puts them
                              there.
  build/next/index.ts         Resources are copied verbatim from src to out by
                              path. workbench.html is already on this list and is
                              how the mechanism is known to work; the media beside
                              it - the narrow, touch and font stylesheets the page
                              links, and the two woff2 they name - go the same way.
                              They cannot be bundled instead: esbuild bundles CSS
                              only for the entry points in
                              getCssBundleEntryPointsForTarget, which would merge
                              them into workbench.css mid-cascade when they are
                              overrides that must come last, and its loader table
                              has no .woff2 entry.

Doing this here rather than copying into the release afterwards is what keeps
build.sh free of a post-build phase, and keeps the overlay a plain mirror of the
source tree with no timing dimension. An upstream bump that restructures either
list fails at fuzz=0, which is exactly when we need to look.

--- a/ci/build/build-release.sh
+++ b/ci/build/build-release.sh
@@ -62,6 +62,8 @@
   mkdir -p "$RELEASE_PATH/src/browser/pages"
   rsync src/browser/pages/*.html "$RELEASE_PATH/src/browser/pages"
   rsync src/browser/pages/*.css "$RELEASE_PATH/src/browser/pages"
+  # Composery: our pages load scripts too; without this they 404 from /_static.
+  rsync src/browser/pages/*.js "$RELEASE_PATH/src/browser/pages"
   rsync src/browser/robots.txt "$RELEASE_PATH/src/browser"
 
   # Adds the commit to package.json
--- a/lib/vscode/build/next/index.ts
+++ b/lib/vscode/build/next/index.ts
@@ -351,6 +351,9 @@
 	'vs/workbench/contrib/extensions/browser/media/*.png',
 	'vs/workbench/services/extensionManagement/common/media/*.svg',
 	'vs/workbench/services/extensionManagement/common/media/*.png',
+
+	// Composery: workbench stylesheets and fonts workbench.html links directly.
+	'vs/code/browser/workbench/media/*',
 ];
 
 // Resources for standalone web target (browser-only, no server)
